                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "Changed the type to sdbusplus::object_path and sdbusplus::object_path isn't a literal type, so it can't be constexpr, changed to static const though."
                },
                {
                    "file": "test/common/events/events.cpp",
                    "line": 224,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "nit: this is just a personal preference but maybe we could reduce the indirection here by inlining the argument and duplicating `testErrorAssertDeAssert`\ninto `testErrorAssertDeAssertVerificationFailed` and `testErrorAssertDeAssertApplyFailed`.\n\nSimilar for `testEventCommit`\n\nThat then cascades into `testAssertEvent` and `testDeAssertEvent` where since the argument is known, these can also be inlined and we avoid a large switch-case and overall indirection, improving the readability of the test code since it is less longer distributed across multiple functions."
                },
